@startuml testing
title How the plugin is tested with trmnlp

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Developer as dev
participant "test/run.js" as run
participant "temp copy of plugin/\n(.trmnlp.yml + src/)" as tmp
participant "trmnlp build" as trmnlp
participant "shared.liquid\n(data + layout, trmnl-liquid filters:\nqr_code, markdown_to_html)" as liquid
participant "test/.cache\n(plugins.css 3.4.0 + fonts)" as cache
participant "Chromium\n(playwright-core)" as chrome
participant "zbarimg" as zbar

== 1. Rendered tests, ~3 minutes ==
dev -> run : node test/run.js [filter]
loop every content case (about 40)
  run -> tmp : copy src/, write .trmnlp.yml\n(custom_fields + webhook "payment" variables)
  opt case.patch (e.g. the server's fixed-size QR svg)
    run -> tmp : rewrite shared.liquid in the copy only
  end
  run -> trmnlp : trmnlp build (cwd = copy)
  trmnlp -> liquid : render full / half_horizontal / half_vertical / quadrant\nwith the settings and webhook "payment"
  liquid --> trmnlp : _build/<view>.html
  trmnlp --> run : 4 HTML files (memoized per case)

  loop every device x view in the case's matrix
    run -> cache : swap trmnl.com CSS/JS and /fonts/ for local copies
    note right of run
      devices: OG, OG portrait, TRMNL X,
      Kindle (screen~--sm), BWRY color, classic
      fonts, dark mode (screen inverted, images not). A half or quarter is a
      slot inside the screen (~--full-w / ~--full-h),
      not a smaller screen.
    end note
    run -> chrome : open page at the device's pixel size\n+ screen~--* classes
    chrome -> chrome : fonts ready, template script\n(accent colors, list marks, text fit)
    run -> chrome : measure(): layout mode, QR box,\ntext rects, overflow, rows, title bar
    chrome --> run : numbers
    run -> chrome : screenshot
    chrome --> run : PNG -> test/shots/
    run -> zbar : decode PNG (-Sbinary)
    zbar --> run : exact QR payload
    run -> run : assertions
    note right of run
      layout chosen = expected (rule written in the test)
      QR scans to exactly the expected payload
      QR modules >= 2 px, quiet zone >= 6 px,
      code fills >= 98 % of its box, still scans in dark mode
      no text off-screen, on the QR or under the title bar
      body text fits, price rows right-aligned and full width
      list items have a mark, dividers, footer not cut,
      title bar text / icon / hidden
    end note
  end
end
run --> dev : "117 passed, 0 failed" + screenshots

== 2. Ship ==
dev -> trmnlp : trmnlp lint, trmnlp push, then trmnlp pull
note right of trmnlp
  the device is the last check: TRMNL's server
  can differ from trmnlp (its qr_code svg had a
  fixed size), so a difference found there
  becomes a new case with a source patch
end note
@enduml
